Theorem DP-1: Decision predicate signatures — pure-state DPs + context-dependent DPs + DP-10 confirmation-of-removal

  Preconditions:
    - Decision predicates map lattice states to logical ownership-event,
      mutation-isolation, and donor/recipient-transfer decisions per Annex E
      §AIMS + Appendix C truth tables
    - Most DPs are pure functions of AimsState; DP-5 + DP-9 additionally
      consult borrow_sources + project_alias_sources + live-variable set
    - MutationObligation is the closed sum type returned by DP-9; CowMode is
      retained only as a historical artifact alias
    - DP-10 was REMOVED from Annex E §AIMS as unsound
      (confirmation-of-removal entry authored below)

  Soundness property:
    Pure-state DP signatures (per Annex E §AIMS + the canonical proof notation:245):

      DP-1 : AimsState -> Bool
        needs_ownership_events(s) <=> s.access = O AND
          s.consumption != empty AND NOT s.is_scalar

      DP-2 : AimsState -> Bool
        is_release_unnecessary(s) <=> s.cardinality = absent OR
          s.consumption = empty

      DP-3 : AimsState -> Bool
        is_additional_credit_elidable(s) <=> s.cardinality = 1 AND
          (s.consumption = L OR s.consumption = A)

      DP-4 : AimsState -> Bool
        needs_sharing_observation(s) <=> s.uniqueness = ms

      DP-6 : AimsState -> Bool
        is_reuse_candidate(s) <=> s.access = O AND s.uniqueness != s AND s.shape != Phi

      DP-7 : AimsState -> Bool
        is_event_pair_elision_eligible(s) <=> s.locality <= fl AND
          s.access = O AND s.consumption = L AND s.cardinality = 1 AND
          s.uniqueness = u AND NOT s.is_scalar

      DP-8 : AimsState -> Bool
        is_local(s) <=> s.locality in {bl, fl}

    Context-dependent DP signatures (per Annex E §AIMS +
    the canonical proof notation:252-256):

      DP-5 : AimsState x ArcVarId x FieldPath x ProgramPoint x InstructionKind -> Bool
        can_mutate_in_place(s, var, field, point, kind) <=>
          s.access = O AND s.uniqueness = u
          AND no_active_overlapping_borrows(var, field, point, kind)

        no_active_overlapping_borrows uses borrow_sources +
        project_alias_sources + live-variable set per Annex E §AIMS
        DP-5 procedure (two-step check: direct borrows + transitive aliases).

        SetTag clause (per Annex E §AIMS RL-10): when kind = SetTag,
        the tag change invalidates ALL payload fields (variant may have
        different layout) -> DP-5 treats SetTag as overlapping every field;
        tag-mutation context blocks whenever ANY borrow is live regardless
        of field path. Signature amended at rule reformulation (case 3) surfaced
        during the DP-5 discharge.

      DP-9 : AimsState x ArcVarId x FieldPath x ProgramPoint x ParamContract
        -> MutationObligation
        mutation_obligation(s, var, field, point, contract) =
          Unique AND DP-5 = true -> SameIdentityAdmissible
          Unique AND DP-5 = false -> IsolationRequired
          MaybeShared AND contract.uniqueness = Unique AND DP-5 = true
            -> SameIdentityAdmissible
          MaybeShared AND contract.uniqueness = Unique AND DP-5 = false
            -> SharingObservationRequired
          MaybeShared else -> SharingObservationRequired
          Shared -> IsolationRequired

        Row (c) joint-DP-5 refinement (per Annex E §AIMS DP-9 row (c)
        + the DP-9 proof artifact): MaybeShared + IC-3 ParamContract.
        uniqueness = Unique routes to SameIdentityAdmissible only when DP-5
        returns true locally; otherwise SharingObservationRequired remains
        (row c-prime). IC-3 proves not-shared at function entry but does
        NOT prove no-active-local-borrows at the mutation point; DP-9 must
        compose IC-3 (interprocedural) with DP-5 (intraprocedural alias
        safety). Signature amended at rule reformulation (case 3) surfaced during
        the DP-9 discharge.

      MutationObligation : closed sum type:
        MutationObligation = SameIdentityAdmissible | IsolationRequired |
          SharingObservationRequired

    DP-10 confirmation-of-removal entry:

      DP-10 — Owned + Linear + Once does NOT imply one logical owner (REMOVED)

      Removed in: Annex E §AIMS DP-10 removal note
        (2026-04 root cause documented inline)

      Root cause: Backward analysis proves "no future duplication" but
        NOT "no existing aliases". Uniqueness is ONLY established via
        the Uniqueness lattice dimension (§AIMS §3.4) OR via fresh allocation
        (TF-3 FRESH output). DP-10's inference from Consumption x Cardinality
        alone was unsound: one use may store the value into a data structure
        and create another logical owner.

      Subsumed by:
        - TF-3 (fresh allocation establishes Uniqueness = u directly)
        - Uniqueness dimension (§AIMS §3.4) as direct source of truth

      No theorem skeleton to discharge; this is a CONFIRMATION entry only.

